R produces executable Rust values E = R(t). The printer P then maps those values back to text,
yielding Treproduced = P(E) = P(R(t)). The conversion is lossless only if Treproduced == t
byte-for-byte; otherwise the benchmark might evaluate the wrong concrete testcase.





